{"repositoryId":582305557,"availability":"available","full":"ikrishg/panasch","name":"panasch","description":"Beautiful Opinionated Logging for Node.js ✍️","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2022-12-26T12:00:14Z","updated":"2026-10-11T19:32:26Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ikrishg.github.io/panasch/","topics":[],"demo":"https://ikrishg.github.io/panasch/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:02.274Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:02.274Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:02.274Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T06:39:02.274Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["TypeScript-first, zero-runtime-dependency JSON logger for Node, Bun, Deno, and edge runtimes. No worker threads and no transport workers—logs serialize synchronously and write to console (or your sink) in-process.","Pino is fast on long-lived Node servers, but its worker-thread transports do not fit short-lived and edge runtimes (Cloudflare Workers, Vercel Edge). Teams also report lost or late logs on Lambda when flushing async transports. Panasch avoids that failure mode by design: no background workers, no separate transport process, no flush race on process exit.","Winston brings a large transport ecosystem at the cost of bundle size, complexity, and uneven TypeScript ergonomics. Panasch targets the same structured JSON shape with a smaller surface and first-class TypeScript types."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ikrishg/panasch/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b14c93b725ba267454630af42f0f9bbe960b14b338e005c036285bde45737668","extractedAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:02.442Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:02.442Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"TypeScript-first, zero-runtime-dependency JSON logger for Node, Bun, Deno, and edge runtimes. No worker threads and no transport workers—logs serialize synchronously and w